course: dictionary
lesson: 1849
title: Cockroach: one word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Cockroach» can mean a large brown or black insect with long feelers, or it can be an insult that calls a person very rude and hateful. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning is meant.
explain: Look for clues. If the sentence talks about insects, legs or crumbs in a kitchen, cockroach means the insect. If someone is being called names, it is the insult. Ask yourself: what word would fit here, and does my meaning still make sense in the sentence?
explain: Notice the forms of the word too. The plural is cockroaches, and in the USA people often shorten it to «roach». Read the whole sentence before you decide what the writer means.
fact: A cockroach is a large brown or black insect with long feelers.
fact: Cockroaches live in warm, dirty places and can spread germs.
fact: A cockroach has six legs and a body in three parts, like all insects.
fact: Cockroaches are tough, but cold, heat and hunger can still kill them.
fact: «Cockroach» can also be an insult for a person who is very rude and hateful.
exercise: «Counting legs sorts them out: ants, beetles, mantises and cockroaches have six legs.» How many legs does a cockroach have? | Four | *Six | Ten | Eight
exercise: «A mouse wants crumbs, a cockroach wants dark damp corners.» Where does a cockroach like to be? | Bright, dry, open fields | Snowy mountain tops | *Dark, damp corners | Sunny beaches
exercise: Tom shouts, «You cockroach!» in the playground to be mean. What does he mean? | *Ella is a rude, hateful person | Ella is very tall | Ella is a cute little insect | Ella has eight legs
test: «A cockroach can live for a while without its head, because it breathes through holes along its body.» How does a cockroach breathe? | It does not breathe at all | *Through holes along its body | Through its mouth only | Through its feelers
test: «Cockroaches are tough but not indestructible.» What does indestructible mean? | *Impossible to destroy | Easy to break | Small and quick | Very old
exam: «Termites are sometimes called white ants but are not ants at all; they are closer to cockroaches.» Which group are termites closer to? | *Cockroaches | Ants | Spiders | Beetles
